# Release Workflow

- This repository is `/Users/sourabhyadav/Documents/Project/fastapi-bright-store`.
- Never use `Cursor`, `AI`, `GPT`, or an agent identity as the Git author,
  committer, commit message author, branch owner, or release label. Preserve
  the configured human Git identity. If it is not a human identity, stop and
  ask for correction before committing.
- All changes must be committed on `uat` first and pushed to the remote `uat`
  branch first.
- Never push directly to `live`/`main` and never merge UAT into live without
  explicit user approval in the current request.
- Before UAT push, run relevant tests, lint, and build checks. Report failures
  instead of claiming deployment success.
- A request such as “live kar do” explicitly authorizes the live workflow:
  verify the current commit is already on remote `uat`, merge/promote it to
  the configured live branch, then deploy that exact commit to the server.
- Live deployment target is `/var/www/html/`. Use the repository's configured
  deployment method and preserve secrets outside the repository.
- Do not run destructive commands on the live server. Do not use
  `rm -rf`, `git reset --hard`, or `rsync --delete` against
  `/var/www/html/` unless the user names the exact action and approves it.
- After a live deployment, run a health check and report the deployed commit,
  target path, result, and any remaining issue.
- If GitHub, SSH, server access, or branch permissions are unavailable, stop
  at that boundary and report the exact blocker; do not bypass it.
